      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62809",
      ":question/problem": "The area, in square meters, of a horizontal cross-section of a water storage tank at height $h$ meters is modeled by the function\n\n$A(h) = \\frac{16}{3 + 0.25h^{2}}$.\n\nWater is pumped into the tank. When the height of the water is $2$ meters, the height is increasing at the rate of $0.5$ meters per hour. Find the rate at which the volume of water in the tank is changing with respect to the time when the height of the water is $2m$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
