      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62836",
      ":question/problem": "The area, in square inches, of a horizontal cross-section of a container at height $h$ inches, is modeled by the function\n\n$A(h) = \\frac{40}{h + 2^{h/3}}$.\n\nA liquid cleaning product is pumped into the container. When the height of the liquid is $3$ inches, the height is increasing at the rate of $0.25$ inches per second. Find the rate at which the volume of the liquid in the container is changing with respect to the time when the height of the liquid is $3in$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
